(MOCK - Tracing a Small Program) Tj T*
(SYNTHETIC LOCAL DEMO - NOT INSTITUTIONAL CONTENT OR APPROVAL) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Objective: Trace an input, two sequential assignments and an output, preserving the) Tj T*
(order of updates.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MOCK ORIGINAL LESSON. A variable is a named place for a current value. Input) Tj T*
(supplies a value, processing changes or combines values, and output reports a) Tj T*
(result. Read instructions from top to bottom. An assignment replaces the old value;) Tj T*
(it does not keep every earlier value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(WORKED EXAMPLE) Tj T*
(Start with count = 2. First run count = count + 3, so count becomes 5. Then run) Tj T*
(count = count * 2, so count becomes 10. Displaying count outputs 10. Reversing the) Tj T*
(two assignments would produce 7, so their order matters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHECK AND CORRECTION) Tj T*
(Which instruction is processing rather than input or output?) Tj T*
(Multiplication transforms the supplied values. Reading and displaying belong to the) Tj T*
(input and output stages.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Before continuing, separate the current value from the instruction. If count is 4,) Tj T*
(the instruction count = count + 2 replaces it with 6. Only the next instruction sees) Tj T*
(that updated 6. Writing the value after every line prevents using the original input) Tj T*
(twice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INDEPENDENT APPLICATION) Tj T*
(Start count = 4. Run count = count + 2, then count = count * 3. What value is) Tj T*
(displayed?) Tj T*
(The addition gives 6; the next line multiplies that 6 by 3 to give 18.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GLOSSARY) Tj T*
(Input: A value supplied to a program before a calculation uses it.) Tj T*
(Variable: A name associated with a current value that assignments may replace.) Tj T*
(Assignment: An instruction that stores a calculated or supplied value in a variable.) Tj T*
(Output: A value or message that the program reports.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To trace a sequence independently, record each new value in order, then report the) Tj T*
(last value at the output instruction. Practice results here are demonstration study) Tj T*
(data, not a course grade.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Original mock fixture. No real learner data, school policy, signatures or) Tj T*
(redistribution review.) Tj T*
(Version 1. Accessible lesson text and authored checks are included separately in) Tj T*
(this package.) Tj T*
